      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:73:35",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ رَجُلٍ ظَاهَرَ مِنِ امْرَأَتِهِ ثُمَّ طَلَّقَهَا قَبْلَ أَنْ يُوَاقِعَهَا فَبَانَتْ مِنْهُ أَ عَلَيْهِ كَفَّارَةٌ قَالَ لَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Mahboub, from Al Aa’la, from Muhammad Bin Muslim who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> about a man who did <span class=\"iTxt\">Zahaar</span> from his wife, then divorced her before he copulated with her. So she was irrevocably divorced from him. Is there an expiation upon him?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "35. Ibn Mahbub has narrated from al-‘ Ala’ from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has said the following: “I once asked abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who expresses the statement of al- Zihar about his wife, then divorces her before going to bed with her until she becomes stranger to him: if he owes expiation. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, expiation is not obligatory on him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
